The HL System is a spatial grammar. These are the things that grammar enables.

---

## Intelligent Systems

**[Robotics Navigation](/concepts/edge-processing)** — An HL-addressed environment gives robots a pre-loaded map. No SLAM required at runtime. No compute overhead for known spaces. The device wakes up, reads the local address, and acts.

**[House Brain](/concepts/house-brain)** — A permanent local AI installed in a home like a furnace. It knows the wiring, the plumbing, the appliance history, the permit records. When owners change, it stays.

**[Home Assistant](/concepts/home-assistant)** — HL addresses map directly to Home Assistant entity IDs. Every switch, sensor, and light gets a stable, human-readable name tied to its physical location.

---

## Record & Continuity

**[Living Provenance](/concepts/living-provenance)** — Objects carry origin records. An item sold at an estate sale can still find its family. The record travels with the object.

**[Living Archive](/concepts/living-archive)** — A home's complete spatial and material record, maintained over time. Not a snapshot. A running log.

---

## Human Extension

**[Human OS](/concepts/human-os)** — The same grammar that addresses a garage can address knowledge, projects, and time.

**[Artist Reward](/concepts/artist-reward)** — A handmade object deserves a record as much as a tractor. HL provenance applied to creative work.

---

## Infrastructure Argument

**[Edge Processing](/concepts/edge-processing)** — Smart home devices currently offload spatial processing to remote servers because local environments lack structure. HL addresses make that round-trip unnecessary.
